@startuml
title ERS Authorization — Account-Level Self-Service vs Tenant Authority

actor "Authenticated Person" as User

rectangle "Authentication Account" as Account
rectangle "Global Person" as Person
rectangle "Person–Tenant Membership" as Membership
rectangle "Tenant Actor" as Actor

rectangle "Base Intrinsic Self-Service" as Self {
  rectangle "Own Person record"
  rectangle "Own previous Earnings"
  rectangle "Own previous Expenses"
}

rectangle "Tenant / Collaborator Capabilities" as Collab {
  rectangle "Tenant workspace"
  rectangle "Current Work Assignments"
  rectangle "Current Earnings / Expenses"
}

rectangle "Delegated Authorization" as Delegated {
  rectangle "Tenant Administrator"
  rectangle "Earnings Operator"
  rectangle "Expenses Operator"
}

User --> Account
Account --> Person
Person --> Self

Person --> Membership
Account --> Actor
Actor --> Membership

Actor --> Collab : when tenant Actor +\nMembership are active
Actor --> Delegated : via Role Grants

note bottom of Self
NOT granted by PERSON Role.

Derived from:
Authentication Account → Person.

Historical financial records retain
their original Tenant provenance.
end note

note bottom of Actor
Tenant Actor activates tenant
operating context. Deactivation
does not remove base Person
self-service.
end note

note bottom of Delegated
Explicit Role / Role Grant.
end note

@enduml
